// ClientPayload Client metadata accepted by the management API. A payload is valid if it is a valid SaaS client payload (ClientMetadata, the body of SaaS POST /oauth2/register) and/or a valid on-prem client payload (DynamicClientRequest, the body of on-prem POST /register, plus the on-prem runtime client properties in OnPremClientFields). These are flat objects with no conflicting property names, so either payload, or a mix of both, can be sent as-is. Where SaaS and on-prem define the same property, the on-prem definition is stricter (enums) and wins. `extension` is the shared DynamicClientExtension (same as SaaS).
